@startuml dsd_uc2_confirmReturn
' NewEra POS - Design sequence diagram, UC2 Handle Returns: confirmReturn() (Contract 8), W11
' Team D - editable source of assets/dsd_uc2_confirmReturn.png
' Render with: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng assets/dsd_uc2_confirmReturn.puml
' Participants: logical view (architecture.md 4.2). Operations: system_interfaces.md 3.3, 3.7, 4.1 to 4.3; AD-05, AD-07, AD-08, AD-09.
' Messages marked <<new>> are not in the logical view or in system_interfaces.md yet (sent to Borja for the design class diagram).
title DSD UC2 Handle Returns - confirmReturn() (Contract 8)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ParticipantPadding 8
skinparam BoxPadding 6
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFBE6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B7791F
skinparam maxMessageSize 190
hide footbox
box "ui.api" #EAF2E3
  participant "ctrl:ReturnController" as C
end box
box "application" #E8EEF7
  participant "h:ReturnHandler" as H
  participant ":PaymentMethods" as PMS
  participant "pm:PaymentMethod" as PM
end box
box "domain" #FFF7E0
  participant "r:Return" as R
  participant "rli:ReturnLineItem" as RLI
  participant "pd:ProductDescription" as PD
end box
box "application.interfaces" #F6EDF7
  participant ":PaymentService" as PAY
  participant ":CashDrawer" as DR
  participant ":Transaction\nRepository" as TR
  participant ":ReceiptPrinter" as PRT
end box

[-> C : POST /api/returns/{returnID}/confirm
C -> H : confirmReturn()
H -> R : refundTotal()
R --> H : amount (at least one line, else 409 "Enter an item")
H -> R : originalPayment()
R --> H : original (the Payment of the sale: tender and payment reference, DR-19)
H -> PMS : get(original.tenderType)
PMS --> H : pm
H -> PM : refund(original, amount, employeeID)
note right of PM : Polymorphism (AD-08): the handler never tests the tender (BR-08, NFR-09).\nThe return has no card reader: the refund uses the payment reference, not the card (AD-09).

alt CASH (9a)
  PM -> DR : open(CASH_REFUND, employeeID)
  DR --> PM : OPENED (logged, IR-14)
  PM --> H : RefundOutcome CASH_PAID
else CREDIT_CARD (9b)
  PM -> PAY : refund(RefundRequest(r.transactionID, original.reference, amount))
  note right of PAY : the adapter applies the 10 s timeout (AD-07);\nthe same transaction ID in every retry (IR-02)
  alt APPROVED
    PAY --> PM : PaymentResult(APPROVED, reference)
    PM --> H : RefundOutcome CARD_REFUNDED (with reference)
  else DECLINED (9b2a)
    PAY --> PM : PaymentResult(DECLINED, reason)
    PM --> H : RefundOutcome NEEDS_APPROVAL (no cash paid)
  else NOT_AVAILABLE: outcome unknown (9b2b)
    PAY --> PM : PaymentResult(NOT_AVAILABLE)
    PM -> PAY : refundStatus(r.transactionID)
    note right of PAY : same transaction ID: the Payment Service says whether the refund was made
    alt APPROVED
      PAY --> PM : APPROVED
      PM --> H : CARD_REFUNDED
    else DECLINED (the refund failed or is unknown)
      PAY --> PM : DECLINED
      PM --> H : NEEDS_APPROVAL
    else NOT_AVAILABLE
      PAY --> PM : NOT_AVAILABLE
      PM --> H : RefundOutcome PENDING (nothing is paid)
    end
  end
else CHECK (9c)
  PM --> H : RefundOutcome NEEDS_APPROVAL (cash only with a store manager, FR-25)
end

H -> R : addRefund(outcome) <<new>>
R -> R : create Refund(tender, amount, state, reference)
note right of R : Creator: the return records its Refund.\nThe reference of a card refund is encrypted when it is saved (AD-09)

alt CASH_PAID, CARD_REFUNDED or PENDING
  H -> R : complete() <<new>>
  loop each ReturnLineItem with condition RESELLABLE
    R -> RLI : restock()
    RLI -> PD : increaseStock(quantity)
    note right of PD : NOT_RESELLABLE: no stock change (FR-23);\nthe item is only recorded
  end
  R -> R : isComplete = true
  R --> H : AccountingRecord
  note right of R : Creator: the return has the data of the record\n(refund, tax refunded, tender, refund state)
  H -> TR : saveCompleted(r, record)
  note right of TR : ONE database transaction (AD-05, AD-06): return, lines, refund, the FIRST row of refund_status\n(state and reference of the refund), stock changes, the AccountingQueue record and the store_sync_list entry.\nPENDING: listed on S-02 (findPendingRefunds, FR-77); checkRefundStatus asks again later. No cash is paid.
  H -> R : getReceipt()
  R --> H : receipt (FR-71, last 4 digits only)
  H -> PRT : print(receipt)
  PRT --> H : READY (NO_PAPER or ERROR: the return is saved, reprint later, IR-13)
  H --> C : ConfirmResult(refund state, receiptNumber,\nprinterStatus, drawerStatus) <<new>>
  C -->[ : 200 CASH_PAID, CARD_REFUNDED or PENDING; receipt number
else NEEDS_APPROVAL (card declined, or check)
  note over H, R : No cash is paid and nothing is saved yet: the Refund stays unpaid and the return stays open (Contract 8).
  H --> C : ConfirmResult(NEEDS_APPROVAL, reason) <<new>>
  C -->[ : 200 NEEDS_APPROVAL: D-01 opens
  ref over C, R : approveCashRefund(managerID, pin, reason), see dsd_uc2_approveCashRefund
end

note over H
  GRASP
  Polymorphism, Protected Variations: one PaymentMethod for each tender behind one interface; a new tender changes no handler (NFR-09, AD-08).
  Creator: Return creates its Refund and its AccountingRecord.
  Information Expert: Return knows the refund total and the tender of the sale; ReturnLineItem knows its condition and restocks only if resellable; ProductDescription changes its own stock level.
  Indirection, Pure Fabrication: PaymentService, CashDrawer, TransactionRepository and ReceiptPrinter are interfaces (DC-02); the timeout is in the adapter, the fallback in the handler (AD-07).
  Low Coupling: the controller only calls the handler.
end note
@enduml
